      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the moment it\u0027s just these 2 pKVM-specific hypercalls. But maybe we want to support some KVM PV hypercalls (e.g. KVM_HC_KICK_CPU, KVM_HC_SEND_IPI, KVM_HC_SCHED_YIELD) for pVM as well?\n\nSo how about modifying kvm_hypercallX() itself instead? Something like:\n\n```\n--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h\n+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h\n@@ -52,6 +52,9 @@ static inline long kvm_hypercall1(unsigned int nr, unsigned long p1)\n \tif (cpu_feature_enabled(X86_FEATURE_TDX_GUEST))\n \t\treturn tdx_kvm_hypercall(nr, p1, 0, 0, 0);\n \n+\tif (pkvm_is_protected_guest())\n+\t\treturn kvm_hypercall4(nr, p1, 0, 0, 0);\n+\n \tasm volatile(KVM_HYPERCALL\n \t\t     : \"\u003da\"(ret)\n \t\t     : \"a\"(nr), \"b\"(p1)\n```\n\n(and similarly in all other kvm_hypercallX() functions)\n\nWe can also make pkvm_is_protected_guest() use a static key?",
      "revId": "406fc146ec01f22636976718afa5a1d48996b477",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
