      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems we need some refactoring if we want to implement like this. The reason is that, we have arch/x86/include/asm/pkvm.h, which declares pkvm_is_protected_guest(actually I will move this as an inline function for using static key). So the asm/kvm_para.h needs to \"#include \u003casm/pkvm.h\u003e\". But the asm/pkvm.h also \"#include \u003casm/kvm_param.h\u003e\". To resolve this interdependent, how about split the pkvm guest related headers from pkvm.h to pkvm_guest.h, so that the asm/kvm_para.h can just \"#include \u003casm/pkvm_guest.h\u003e\" which will not have the interdependent issue?\n\nAnd if we use the above snapshot by calling kvm_hypercall4 directly, then seems we don\u0027t need to define our pkvm_guest_hypercall, but just declare kvm_hypercall4 in the front, right?",
      "parentUuid": "3d1c4dbf_a451e922",
      "revId": "406fc146ec01f22636976718afa5a1d48996b477",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
